  "goodToKnow": "Der Pudel is a poodle, originally a German water dog for hunting ducks; its name comes from pudeln, to splash. In Goethe's Faust, the devil Mephisto first appears as a black poodle, giving the idiom des Pudels Kern (the heart of the matter). Wie ein begossener Pudel means crestfallen. Die Pudelmütze is a bobble hat, and sich pudelwohl fühlen means to feel on top of the world. The plural is the same."
